[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station approx. 36m wide at bankfull. GENERAL: Velocity area station approx. 36m wide at bankfull. Important flood forecasting station. STATION HYDROMETRY: Downstream shoal acts as a control, but shoal and rating are not too stable. All but extreme flows contained. Four peak flow ratings applied over period of record. Spot gauged close to highest flow in record. FLOW RECORD: Analomous flows in Aug/Sept 1975. The pre-1976 data is thought to be less reliable due to inconsistencies over the way the datum change has been handled. FLOW REGIME: Quite responsive. Flows substantially affected by Derwent reservoirs.
CATCHMENT,Upland catchment with peat covered moorlands in the headwaters. Geology: predominantly Millstone Grit, with some western tributaries draining Carboniferous Limestone. Predominantly pasture.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged beyond AMAX3. Good fit to gaugings.
[END]
